From: CoverSurface <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: sun8i: do not fail the probe on the external-PHY reset

The AC200 EPHY on the Remix Mini PC only drives the RMII clocks once phylib
has attached and resumed it, which happens on open, not during probe. The
probe-time soft reset then times out and the whole device is torn down,
although the MAC works fine once the interface is opened.

Warn and carry on instead.

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -1226,9 +1226,10 @@ static int sun8i_dwmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			goto dwmac_mux;
 		}
 	} else {
+		/* ponytail: an external PHY may not clock the MAC until open */
 		ret = sun8i_dwmac_reset(priv);
 		if (ret)
-			goto dwmac_remove;
+			dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "probe-time reset failed, continuing\n");
 	}
 
 	pm_runtime_put(&pdev->dev);
